meta {
  name: 69 Branch Role Permissions
  seq: 69
}

docs {
  # Branch × Role Permissions (tier-2)

  The branch-level role permission overrides — the layer between the static
  role baseline (code templates) and per-user overrides
  (`user_branch_permissions`). Effective resolution (in `GET
  /users/manage/me/permissions`): **user override ?? branch-role override ??
  role baseline**.

  Managed under `permissions/branch-roles` (business-authenticated; tenant +
  actor from the JWT):

  - **GET `/grid`** — the full Branch × Role cartesian for the tenant (every
    branch × every role), each row with `overriddenCount`. Business Admin.
  - **GET `/:branchId/:authRoleId`** — the module-grouped permissions for one
    (branch + role): `baseline` (role template) + `allowed` (branch-role
    override ?? baseline), gated by the branch's enabled modules.
  - **PUT `/:branchId/:authRoleId`** — replace that (branch + role)'s overrides
    (full desired set; Select-All / Deselect-All). Audited under
    `AuditModule.USER`.

  Branch scoping: a Business Admin (tenant-level context, `active_branch_id`
  null) may target any branch; a Branch Admin (branch-level context) may only
  target its own active branch (else 403 `BRANCH_SCOPE_VIOLATION`).
}
